Keyword macro expansion and original kernel replay, 2026-09-16.

Minimal source:
  #define inline inline __attribute__((__gnu_inline__))
  inline int f(int x) { return x; }
Before repair, preprocessing lost the attribute and the ISO-inline classifier
omitted f. The RED asserts token expansion and linkable definition role;
all keywords now use the existing preprocessing-identifier predicate during
macro lookup, argument expansion and rescan. Unexpanded tokens retain their
C keyword kind; self references still carry the expansion-inhibition flag.
Controls cover extern, static, nested attribute macros, function-like keyword
names across replacement boundaries, #if, and mutually recursive names.

