These are targeted compile/assembly/symbol checks, not device runtime tests.
After K1 begins forwarding the written -funsigned-char explicitly, each of
these three original commands is replayed once more: all succeed and emit
byte-identical assembly to the hashes above. Commands/deltas are preserved in
.build/vector-targeted/scsi-inline-replay/explicit-options.json. This verifies
that particular default-equivalence; it does not justify dropping signedness
options in general or rewriting old measurement provenance.

Separate measurement-path repair: explicit /usr/ include options can name
the existing exported toolchain root; the order and option spelling remain,
and its bytes participate in input/cache identity. K1 harness: 158 PASS.
The 44 files in GCC-14's compiler include directory match the sealed image
byte for byte. xor-neon.o now reaches arm_neon.h:44 (__Float16x4_t), E1001;
that is a remaining nominal target-type/intrinsic capability, not an FP
execution classification. E0105 was a path projection failure.
The wider 3,492-file export check found eight case-colliding UAPI names with
different bytes on the host (xt_CONNMARK, xt_DSCP, xt_MARK, xt_RATEEST,
xt_TCPMSS, ipt_ECN, ipt_TTL, ip6t_HL). Do not claim that entire export is
byte-identical; the affected compiler include directory is identical.
